/*!
    \qmlmodule VSMM.ModStore
    \title VSMM.ModStore QML Module
    \brief The installed mods and every change to them except adding one.
*/

/*!
    \qmltype ModStore
    \nativetype vsmm::ModStore
    \inqmlmodule VSMM.ModStore
    \brief Installed mods, their selection, updates and removal.

    Adding a mod goes through \l {ModLoader::load()}{ModLoader.load()}
    instead. The \c id argument of every method is the \c modId role of
    \l [QML] {ModListModel}.

    \qml
    Button {
        enabled: !ModStore.workPending && ModStore.updatesCount > 0
        onClicked: ModStore.updateAll()
    }
    \endqml

    Only the change signals of the properties below are meant for QML. The
    other signals are used between the backend libraries.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty int ModStore::installedModsCount
    \readonly
    Number of installed mods.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty int ModStore::updatesCount
    \readonly
    Number of installed mods with an update available. Shares its change
    signal with \l installedModsCount and \l enabledModsCount.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty int ModStore::enabledModsCount
    \readonly
    Number of installed mods that are not disabled in the game's
    \c clientsettings.json. Changes when mods are added or removed, and when
    \l {GameMngr::disabledMods}{GameMngr.disabledMods} changes.

    \sa {GameMngr::addDisabledMod()}{GameMngr.addDisabledMod()},
        {GameMngr::removeDisabledMod()}{GameMngr.removeDisabledMod()}
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty bool ModStore::workPending
    \readonly
    \c true while an update or a reload runs. Starts as \c true and turns
    \c false 500 ms after the first scan and its online info requests
    finish. It stays \c true while
    \l {pathSettings::gameConfig}{Config.paths.gameConfig} is empty or
    missing at startup.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty bool ModStore::modsSelected
    \readonly
    \c true when at least one mod is marked for update.

    \sa markForUpdate()
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void ModStore::reload()
    Drops all mods and scans the mods folders again. Sets \l workPending.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void ModStore::update(string id)
    Updates the mod \a id. Does nothing when the mod has no update or
    \l workPending is \c true.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void ModStore::updateAll()
    Updates every mod with an available update. Does nothing while
    \l workPending is \c true.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void ModStore::updateSelected()
    Updates the mods marked with markForUpdate() that have an update. Does
    nothing while \l workPending is \c true.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void ModStore::markForUpdate(string id, bool marked)
    Marks or unmarks the mod \a id for updateSelected(), depending on
    \a marked. Changes \l modsSelected and the \c isMarkedForUpdate role.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void ModStore::setFavorite(string id, bool favorite)
    Sets whether the mod \a id is a favorite, depending on \a favorite. The
    favorites are saved to \c config.json right away.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void ModStore::remove(string id)
    Deletes the zip of the mod \a id from disk and removes the mod from the
    store and its row from \l [QML] {ModListModel}. The file is deleted, not moved to the trash.
*/
